+### Pre-Dispatch Baseline
+
+Before dispatching the first implementer wave, verify the baseline in the
+main workspace:
+
+1. **Project setup:** dependencies installed, build works (`npm install`,
+   `cargo build`, … as the project demands).
+2. **Clean test baseline:** run the project's test suite. If tests fail,
+   report failures and ask whether to proceed or investigate — otherwise
+   new bugs are indistinguishable from pre-existing ones.
+
+Report before wave 1:
+
+```
+Baseline clean (<N> tests, 0 failures)
+Ready to dispatch isolated implementers for <feature-name>
+```
+
+### Wave Scheduling
+
+- The plan's Dependency Map defines the waves: a task is ready when every
+  task it depends on is merged. Dispatch ALL ready tasks in one batch of
+  implementer subagents — never serialize independent tasks.
+- `isolated: true` is set explicitly on EVERY implementer item. The task
+  tool requires the `isolated` field, and it is not implicit: an item with
+  `isolated: false` edits your worktree directly. Isolated subagents cannot
+  conflict while running.
+- Each isolated implementer's changes come back parked on a task ref; your
+  worktree stays clean while implementers run. Merging refs is governed by
+  the always-applied `isolated-task-merge` rule.
